    "title": "Man accused of kicking deputy - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Staff Writer ,\n7 hours ago\nMARATHON — A 30-year-old local man was arrested Sunday, Sept. 7, for allegedly kicking a Monroe County Sheriff’s Office deputy following an incident at a bar.\nZachary Thomas McDaniel Cappetta was charged with assault on a law enforcement officer, battery on a law enforcement officer, resisting arrest with violence, disorderly intoxication and disorderly conduct.\nDeputies were called to the Brass Monkey bar in Marathon at 2:36 a.m. regarding a disturbance. Cappetta, who was intoxicated, grabbed a woman by the arm, and a man intervened and escorted Cappetta outside, whereupon Cappetta began hitting the man in the face, reports say.\nThe man took Cappetta to the ground and held them there until deputies arrived.\nCappetta resisted deputies, kicking one multiple times in the abdomen, reports say. He was taken to jail.",
